#### 7. Sensitive Equality — `toStringFormat` (line 85)

```java
assertEquals("Catalog(items=1)", catalog.toString());
```

This couples the test to the exact `toString` format string. Any cosmetic change (e.g., adding a space, renaming the field label) breaks the test even though behavior is unchanged.

**Refactor:** Assert on the semantic property, not the string representation:

```java
@Test
void toStringContainsItemCount() {
    catalog.add("a", 1);
    assertTrue(catalog.toString().contains("1"));
}
```

Or better — test `quantity`/`inStock` directly and don't test `toString` at all unless it's part of the public contract.

**Risk if unfixed:** Brittle test that breaks on harmless formatting changes.

