#### 8. Exception Handling — `addNullSkuManualCatch` (line 92)

```java
try {
    catalog.add(null, 1);
    fail("should have thrown");
} catch (Exception ex) {
    assertNotNull(ex.getMessage());
}
```

Manual `try`/`catch`/`fail` is verbose and error-prone (e.g., catching `Exception` instead of the specific type). JUnit 5's `assertThrows` is purpose-built for this.

**Refactor:**

```java
@Test
void addNullSkuThrows() {
    IllegalArgumentException ex = assertThrows(
        IllegalArgumentException.class,
        () -> catalog.add(null, 1));
    assertTrue(ex.getMessage().contains("sku is required"));
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Over-broad `catch` can swallow unexpected exceptions, hiding bugs.

